CVE-2026-21728 exp:2026-09-12


# CVE-2026-34040: Moby authorization bypass.
# Carriers (generated 2026-08-19):
#   gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:v0.52.1, grafana/alloy:v1.18.1
# Each is a pinned third-party image we cannot rebuild, so the fix
# only reaches us when the publisher ships a new tag.
# Why not exploitable: Promtail does not manage Docker daemon authorization or
# sockets directly in our deployment. cAdvisor is a read-only client of the
# Docker API (container list/inspect/stats only, mounts /var/run read-only) —
# it never runs a Docker daemon or authorization-plugin-gated API of its own,
# so a bypass in that server-side logic isn't triggered by cAdvisor's own code.
CVE-2026-34040 exp:2026-09-12

# CVE-2026-28377: Info disclosure in Tempo.
# Carriers (generated 2026-08-19): grafana/grafana:13.0.6-ubuntu.
# Each is a pinned third-party image we cannot rebuild, so the fix
# only reaches us when the publisher ships a new tag.
# Why not exploitable: Tempo integration is not deployed or used in our configuration.
CVE-2026-28377 exp:2026-09-12


# CVE-2026-41567: Container archive execution in Docker.
# Carriers (generated 2026-08-19):
#   gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:v0.52.1, grafana/alloy:v1.18.1
# Each is a pinned third-party image we cannot rebuild, so the fix
# only reaches us when the publisher ships a new tag.
# Why not exploitable: Promtail has no access to the Docker API socket in our
# production deployment. cAdvisor's Docker socket mount is read-only and it
# only ever calls read-only stats/inspect endpoints — it never calls the
# archive/copy endpoints (ContainerArchive / CopyToContainer) this CVE affects.
CVE-2026-41567 exp:2026-09-12

# CVE-2026-42306: Race condition in docker cp.
